<header><p class="enc-kicker">Person</p><h1 class="enc-title">John Kirk</h1><p class="enc-meta"><span class="dates">1832–1922</span> · <a href="/centuries/19th-century">19th century</a> · Also known as Sir John Kirk</p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">Sir John Kirk was a Scottish physician and naturalist who accompanied <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/david-livingstone">David Livingstone</a> on his <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/zambezi">Zambezi</a> expedition and later served as British consul and agent in Zanzibar from 1866 to 1887. His close influence over <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/sultan">Sultan</a> Barghash helped secure the treaty of 1873 that closed the Zanzibar slave market and extended British power on the East African coast.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/john-kirk.jpg" alt="John Kirk" width="320" height="495" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: Unknown authorUnknown author · Public domain · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:JohnKirk1908.jpg" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
